From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: bind multicast sender and receiver to loopback

Source: https://github.com/radarsat1/liblo/releases/tag/0.36
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Applicable-Version: 0.36
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (test-environment adaptation; automated upstream writes forbidden)
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

The package build runs without an external network interface.  The upstream
multicast test asks the kernel to join its group on INADDR_ANY, which fails
with ENODEV in that network namespace even though its loopback interface is
available and supports IPv4 multicast membership.

Use liblo's public interface-selection APIs to bind both sides of the same
multicast test to 127.0.0.1.  This keeps the multicast join, send, receive,
handler, reply, and byte-count assertions intact, and it does not skip or
replace any of the four registered upstream test programs.

Remove this patch when upstream selects an available interface for its
multicast self-test or the locked build network exposes an interface that
allows the unqualified INADDR_ANY membership to succeed.

---
 src/testlo.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/testlo.c b/src/testlo.c
--- a/src/testlo.c
+++ b/src/testlo.c
@@ -784,8 +784,10 @@ void test_multicast(lo_server_thread st)
 
     /* test multicast server and sender */
     /* message is sent from st otherwise reply doesn't work */
-    ms = lo_server_new_multicast("224.0.1.1", "15432", error);
+    ms = lo_server_new_multicast_iface("224.0.1.1", "15432", NULL,
+                                       "127.0.0.1", error);
     ma = lo_address_new("224.0.1.1", "15432");
+    TEST(lo_address_set_iface(ma, NULL, "127.0.0.1") == 0);
     lo_address_set_ttl(ma, 1);
     lo_server_add_method(ms, "/foo/bar", "fi", foo_handler, ms);
     lo_server_add_method(ms, "/reply", "s", reply_handler, NULL);
